{
  "name": "blstrs",
  "description": "A high-performance Rust implementation of the BLS12-381 pairing-friendly elliptic curve construction, utilizing the blst library as a low-level assembly backend. It provides efficient G1, G2, and GT group operations, including bilinear pairings through optimized Miller loops and final exponentiation over a tower of extension fields up to Fp12. The library is specifically engineered for zk-SNARK applications, featuring constant-time execution and support for hardware-accelerated operations via GPU and specialized architectures.",
